    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald are delighted to present No. 16 Hollywoodrath Road to the market. Ideally located opposite a large green area, No. 16 is a beautifully presented 5 bedroomed detached family home, built in 2016. The property is in a highly desirable location close to shops, schools and public transport to the city centre and surrounding areas. The property benefits from a versatile attic conversion with en-suite, which is an additional 33 sq.m approx. of versatile accommodation, that could be used as a bedroom, home office, playroom or gym.\n \nOn entering the home, you are welcomed into the bright and spacious hallway with stairs leading to first floor landing opening to both the living room, kitchen/dining room, playroom and downstairs WC. The living room is a fantastic entertaining space, with bay window to front aspect, built in media wall, feature electric fire. The playroom seamlessly flows through double doors into the open plan kitchen and dining room area. The open plan kitchen/dining room is a great space for family dinners and entertaining. The kitchen itself is fitted with soft grey base/wall units with sizeable worktops, built in island, inset sink with mixer tap. From the kitchen there is also a sizable utility room, fitted with base units and space for washing machine and dryer. \n \nUpstairs, there are three generous double bedrooms, all with fitted wardrobes, with the master bedroom benefiting from an en-suite shower room. The fourth bedroom is a sizable single room. The family bathroom is well-appointed with a bath, dual-head shower, wash hand basin, WC, heated towel rail, and stylish partially tiled walls and flooring.\n \nOutside to the front of the property there is a sizable driveway for two cars with a side lawned area. Double gated side access to the enclosed private rear garden which is laid in lawn with a patio area and outdoor tap. \n \nThis home combines practical family living, stylish finishes, and a highly convenient location, making it a truly exceptional property\n \nHollywoodrath Road is a peaceful, affluent estate, with a good selection of shopping and leisure facilities both locally and within a ten-minute drive. There is easy access to the city centre, N3/M3/M50, Blanchardstown Shopping Centre, and Dublin Airport."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 4.39m x 2m\nWelcoming hallway finished with stylish acoustic wall panelling. Features staircase with runner carpet, stair lighting and spot lighting.\n\nLiving Room - 3.94m x 3.9m\nStylish living room featuring an electric fire set within a bespoke media unit, complemented by acoustic wall panelling. The room is finished with laminate flooring and benefits from a bay window to the front, offering pleasant views overlooking the green area.\n\nPlayroom - 3.88m x 3.48m\nFeaturing laminate flooring. Double doors open through to the kitchen/dining room, creating an ideal family-friendly flow between spaces.\n\nWC - 1.5m x1.4m\nConveniently located guest bathroom with tiled flooring, a WC and wash hand basin.\n\nPantry - 2m x 1.67m\n\n\nKitchen/ Dinning Room - 6.4m x 5.26m\nSpacious and light-filled kitchen/dining area featuring laminate flooring and two skylights allowing natural light flow through out. The kitchen is fitted with a tiled splashback, electric four-ring hob, oven, and integrated wine rack. A central island provides additional workspace and incorporates a dual sink with drainer and modern mixer tap.\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.1m x 3.35m\nLarge double bedroom located to the front of the property and fully fitted wardrobes. Laminate flooring.\n\nEn-Suite - \nEn-Suite Comprises of, shower unit, wc, wash hand basin and heated towel rail. Partly tiled walls and tiled flooring.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.02m x 2.97m\nGenerous sized double bedroom to the rear of the house with fully fitted wardrobes. Laminate flooring.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.3m x 2.85m\nGood sized double bedroom to the rear of the house with built in wardrobes. Laminate flooring.\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.9m x 2.8m\nGenerous sized single bedroom to the front of the house with built in wardrobes. Laminate flooring.\n\nBathroom - 3.3m x 2.05m\nWell-appointed bathroom comprising a bath and a shower unit with dual heads, including a rain shower. Features include a wash hand basin, WC, heated towel rail and partially tiled walls and flooring.\n\nAttic room - \nVersatile attic room offering potential as an additional reception space, home office, gym or playroom. Fitted with skylights for natural light, laminate flooring and access to eaves storage.\n\nGarden - \nPrivate, south-facing rear garden, laid in lawn with a porcelain tiled patio area, ideal for al fresco dining and entertaining in the summer months. The garden is surrounded with composite fencing and benefits from two side access gates.\n\n"
      },
